  "content": {
    "id": "p58-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n\n$$\\dfrac{\\dfrac xy+\\dfrac yx}{4-\\dfrac1{xy}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x^2+y^2}{4xy-1}$, $x\\ne0$, $y\\ne0$, $4xy\\ne1$.",
      "worked": "Multiply the top and bottom by $xy$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\dfrac{\\dfrac xy+\\dfrac yx}{4-\\dfrac1{xy}}&=\\dfrac{xy(\\dfrac xy+\\dfrac yx)}{xy(4-\\dfrac1{xy})}\\\\\\dfrac{\\dfrac xy+\\dfrac yx}{4-\\dfrac1{xy}}&=\\dfrac{x^2+y^2}{4xy-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne0$, $y\\ne0$ and $4xy\\ne1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
